LC 75 — Sort Colors
Pattern:Two Pointers

Logic:
We have 0, 1, 2.

0 → move to front
2 → move to end
1 → stay in middle

Algorithm
l = 0, r = n-1, i = 0
If nums[i] == 0 → swap with l, move both.
If nums[i] == 2 → swap with r, move r only.
If 1 → move i.

CODE:

class Solution {
public:
    void sortColors(vector<int>& a) {
        int l = 0, i = 0, r = a.size()-1;
        while (i <= r) {
            if (a[i] == 0) swap(a[i++], a[l++]);
            else if (a[i] == 2) swap(a[i], a[r--]);
            else i++;
        }
    }
};

EX:
[2,0,2,1,1,0]

0 → swap to front
[0,2,2,1,1,0]

2 → swap to end
[0,1,2,1,2,0]

continue...

[0,0,1,1,2,2] ✅
